  "method": "For each prime p in PRIMES, enumerate every Gaussian residue c in Z[i]/(p) and run the iteration z_{k+1} = z_k^2 + c starting from z_0 = 0 until the orbit revisits a state. Record (preperiod tau, period rho). Render the rho-field as a p x p heatmap (viridis, sqrt-norm). Julia variant fixes c and varies the starting state. Classical Mandelbrot rendered via standard escape time over C for visual comparison.",
  "notes": [
    "Z[i]/(p) is F_{p^2} when p = 3 (mod 4); F_p x F_p when p = 1 (mod 4); F_4 when p = 2.",
    "The naive C_p-Mandelbrot for z^2+c is the closed unit disk (|c|_p <= 1) and carries no fractal boundary; the genuinely fractal non-archimedean structure lives on the Berkovich tree.",
    "The mod-p period heatmap is NOT a coarse approximation of the classical Mandelbrot set. The equidistribution theorem (Baker-Rumely / Favre-Rivera-Letelier) applies to roots of Misiurewicz polynomials Phi_n - Phi_m, lifted to algebraic numbers, not to the raw period field."
  ]
